# MCO Features - Research Assistant Example
# This file contains optional features that are injected at strategic points in the workflow

@optional Data visualization
>When appropriate, create charts or graphs to visualize key data points or trends.
>Use visualization to highlight comparisons, trends over time, or proportional relationships.
>Consider using bar charts for comparisons, line charts for trends, and pie charts for proportions.

@optional Counterarguments
>Include a section addressing potential counterarguments or alternative perspectives.
>Present opposing viewpoints fairly and address their strengths and weaknesses.
>This adds depth and credibility to the research by showing awareness of different perspectives.

@optional Future implications
>Discuss potential future implications or developments related to the topic.
>Consider how current trends might evolve and what new challenges or opportunities might emerge.
>This helps readers understand the longer-term significance of the research.

@optional Case studies
>Incorporate relevant case studies or examples that illustrate key points.
>Choose diverse examples that show how concepts apply in different contexts.
>Provide enough detail for readers to understand the relevance without overwhelming them.

@optional Comparative analysis
>Include a comparative analysis of different approaches or solutions.
>Create a structured comparison using consistent criteria across all options.
>Highlight relative strengths and weaknesses to help readers make informed decisions.

@brainstorm
>Consider including a section on emerging technologies in the agent orchestration space.
>Explore the relationship between agent orchestration and other AI fields like reinforcement learning.
>Investigate how different industries are applying agent orchestration to solve domain-specific problems.
>Look into the ethical considerations of autonomous agent systems and how orchestration can address them.